WEBVTT

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:17.292
- Who is it?
- Hello.

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:19.500
I'm looking for Montgomery Clyde.

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:21.750
- Never heard of him.
- But you must have done.

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:23.875
I've tried them all
and you're the last...

00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:25.667
Why don't you clear off?

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.208
And if you ever make it to London,

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:40.333
you can be sure of a very warm welcome.

00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:55.167
Ah!

00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:58.292
Please, please, please, please...

00:01:00.208 --> 00:01:01.667
- Hello?
- Hello.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:06.542
- I'm looking for Montgomery Clyde.- Well, that's my father.

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:10.833
- The explorer Montgomery Clyde?- That's right.

00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.583
Come on in out of the cold.
I'll be right down.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:16.875
Oh. Oh, thank you. Thank you!

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.042
Ls Captain Clyde at home?

00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:21.833
I'm afraid not.

00:01:22.292 --> 00:01:25.125
You see, my father is dead.

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:28.458
Oh.

00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:30.417
Oh, dear.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.375
What did you want from him?

00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:38.292
He once told my aunt that if ever
we came to London, we'd be welcome.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.458
And I suppose I hoped
he might give me a home.

00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:46.792
Oh, but I can do that.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.708
- You can?
- Of course.

00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:53.875
A lovely specimen like you
shouldn't be out on the streets.

00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:57.542
You belong somewhere very special.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.750
And I know just the place.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.042
Come along.
We're going for a lovely ride.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:06.625
Miss Clyde!

00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.583
Mr Curry. What do you want?

00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:13.167
I found these tied to a lamppost
and I thought waste not, want not.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.208
Charming. Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.167
Erm... where exactly are you going?

00:02:21.083 --> 00:02:23.042
What concern is it of yours?

00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:27.125
- You've got the bear in there.
- And?

00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:30.167
It's just, I thought you were
sending him to Peru. But...

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.667
I said I was sending him
where he belongs,

00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:35.208
which in his case
is the Natural History Museum.

00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:38.250
But, Honeypot, that is barbaric.

00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:40.958
Mr Curry, I am not your Honeypot.
I never was.

00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:42.292
What?

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:46.375
Now take your rotten ﬂowers
and get out of here! Go.

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:49.042
Run!

00:02:53.792 --> 00:02:55.583
- Hello?- Good evening.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:59.125
This is an anonymous phone call.

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:02.125
- Oh, hello, Mr Curry.
- It's not Mr Curry! It's Mr...

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:04.417
..Burry.

00:03:04.542 --> 00:03:06.583
I have some news

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.333
concerning the bear.

00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:13.125
What? What do you mean?

00:03:13.208 --> 00:03:15.833
- Who is it, Henry?
- It's Mr Curry doing a silly voice.

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:17.083
It's Burry!

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.083
He says Paddington's been kidnapped!

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:45.875
Oh!

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.042
Welcome to your new home, bear.

00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:52.042
This is a cathedral of knowledge.

00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:54.750
Every major explorer
has added to its glory.

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.667
Charles Darwin brought
the giant tortoise from the Galapagos.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.750
Good evening.

00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:01.458
Captain Scott,
the emperor penguin from Antarctica.

00:04:01.542 --> 00:04:03.042
- Gentlemen.
- Captain Cook,

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.083
- the kangaroo from Australia.
- G'day.

00:04:05.292 --> 00:04:08.250
Each of these men has been immortalized
through his finds.

00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:10.500
But do you see anything from my father?

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.042
No.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.333
Because when he met
your oh-so-precious species,

00:04:16.375 --> 00:04:18.625
he refused to collect a specimen.

00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:21.292
No specimen?

00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:24.583
Gentlemen, these were no dumb beasts.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.750
They were intelligent and civilized.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.250
Come off it, Clyde.
They didn't even speak English.

00:04:29.458 --> 00:04:31.500
- Well, no, but...
- Did they play cricket?

00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:33.958
- Drink tea?
- Do the crossword?

00:04:34.042 --> 00:04:36.500
Pretty rum idea of civilization
you've got, Clyde.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:40.333
Tell us their location. We'll send
a real explorer to get a specimen.

00:04:42.292 --> 00:04:43.292
Never!

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.208
Very well.
You leave me no choice.

00:04:46.333 --> 00:04:48.875
This expedition
shall be struck from the records.

00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:51.750
Montgomery Clyde,

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:55.917
I hereby revoke your membership
of this hallowed guild.

00:04:56.167 --> 00:05:00.458
Geographers, turn your backs!

00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:05.375
He could have been rich and famous,

00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:09.708
but instead he threw it all away
and he opened a petting zoo.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.375
He put the happiness
of a few furry creatures

00:05:13.458 --> 00:05:15.083
above his own ﬂesh and blood.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:19.333
I vowed that one day I would finish
the job my father never could.

00:05:20.417 --> 00:05:24.917
And now, at last, that day has come.

00:05:33.875 --> 00:05:35.375
That's right!

00:05:35.417 --> 00:05:37.833
I'm going to stuff you, bear.

00:05:50.042 --> 00:05:51.417
Ow!

00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:06.167
I see him. And there's not
a moment to lose!

00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:09.208
How are we going to get in?
It'll be locked up like a fortress.

00:06:09.292 --> 00:06:12.917
Sewers. Didn't you say they could
take you anywhere in the city?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.208
Brilliant!

